{
  "_comment": "Governance contracts read on Ethereum mainnet, one entry per governance system; mapping.json says which system decides over which protocol version. Every value on the site comes from one of the `reads` listed here, so a reviewer can repeat it: open the contract's address on Etherscan (Contract → Read), call the view named in `call` with the `args` listed, and compare. `source` is the protocol's own address registry the addresses were taken from; every read answered on-chain on 2026-10-19. Each contract has a `type` — timelock, governor (a token vote), aragon-voting (a token vote), dual-governance (a holder veto), safe, holder (a contract whose privileged role is read), registry, council — and, where a token votes, `token`; the page lists who decides from these. `voting`, on a system whose token holders vote where no contract reports it (Snapshot) or not at all, says so and links the place; the adapter appends it to the note, it is never a value. Fields of a read: `call` — the Solidity signature as `cast sig` takes it (a list when one fact needs two views: a Safe's threshold and its owner list); `args` — the arguments in order (a number for a uint, a 0x… word for bytes32, `$previousBlock` for the block before the one the run reads at); `word` — which 32-byte word of the answer is read when the view returns a tuple (0 by default); `as` — how that word reads: `seconds` (a uint, shown as `N s (readable)`), `count` (a uint with `unit`), `tokens` (a uint divided by 1e18, with `unit` the token symbol), `percent` (Aragon's 1e18 = 100%), `address`, `account` (an address, after which eth_getCode and the Safe views getThreshold()/getOwners() are called on it to say whether it is an EOA, a Safe with its threshold, or another contract), `enum` (a uint index into `values`), `signers` (getThreshold() of getOwners().length); `fact` — the name the value appears under; `headline: true` — the delay the headline reports, in seconds (where two delays apply one after the other, as at Lido, both are marked and the headline is their sum).",
  "aave-governance-v3": {
    "name": "Aave Governance V3",
    "source": "https://github.com/bgd-labs/aave-address-book/blob/main/src/GovernanceV3Ethereum.sol",
    "contracts": [
      {
        "label": "Payloads Controller",
        "address": "0xdAbad81aF85554E9ae636395611C58F7eC1aAEc5",
        "type": "timelock",
        "reads": [
          {
            "call": "getExecutorSettingsByAccessControl(uint8)",
            "args": [1],
            "word": 1,
            "as": "seconds",
            "fact": "Executor level 1 delay",
            "headline": true
          },
          {
            "call": "getExecutorSettingsByAccessControl(uint8)",
            "args": [1],
            "word": 0,
            "as": "address",
            "fact": "Executor level 1"
          },
          {
            "call": "getExecutorSettingsByAccessControl(uint8)",
            "args": [2],
            "word": 1,
            "as": "seconds",
            "fact": "Executor level 2 delay"
          },
          {
            "call": "getExecutorSettingsByAccessControl(uint8)",
            "args": [2],
            "word": 0,
            "as": "address",
            "fact": "Executor level 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Governance V3",
        "address": "0x9AEE0B04504CeF83A65AC3f0e838D0593BCb2BC7",
        "type": "governor",
        "token": "AAVE",
        "reads": [
          {
            "call": "getVotingConfig(uint8)",
            "args": [1],
            "word": 1,
            "as": "seconds",
            "fact": "Level 1 voting duration"
          },
          {
            "call": "getVotingConfig(uint8)",
            "args": [1],
            "word": 2,
            "as": "count",
            "unit": "AAVE",
            "fact": "Level 1 yes threshold"
          },
          {
            "call": "getVotingConfig(uint8)",
            "args": [1],
            "word": 4,
            "as": "count",
            "unit": "AAVE",
            "fact": "Level 1 proposition power required"
          },
          {
            "call": "getVotingConfig(uint8)",
            "args": [2],
            "word": 1,
            "as": "seconds",
            "fact": "Level 2 voting duration"
          },
          {
            "call": "getVotingConfig(uint8)",
            "args": [2],
            "word": 2,
            "as": "count",
            "unit": "AAVE",
            "fact": "Level 2 yes threshold"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Protocol Guardian",
        "address": "0x2CFe3ec4d5a6811f4B8067F0DE7e47DfA938Aa30",
        "type": "safe",
        "reads": [
          {
            "call": ["getThreshold()", "getOwners()"],
            "as": "signers",
            "fact": "Protocol Guardian"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Governance Guardian",
        "address": "0xCe52ab41C40575B072A18C9700091Ccbe4A06710",
        "type": "safe",
        "reads": [
          {
            "call": ["getThreshold()", "getOwners()"],
            "as": "signers",
            "fact": "Governance Guardian"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Risk Council",
        "address": "0x47c71dFEB55Ebaa431Ae3fbF99Ea50e0D3d30fA8",
        "type": "safe",
        "reads": [
          {
            "call": ["getThreshold()", "getOwners()"],
            "as": "signers",
            "fact": "Risk Council"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
